4. OPEN SOURCE AND THIRD-PARTY COMPLIANCE
-----------------------------------------
This software integrates third-party open-source components, which remain under their own licenses and are not covered by the terms above.
* The virtual camera filter in vendor/softcam is the Softcam library by tshino, released under the MIT License (see vendor/softcam/LICENSE). It embeds the DirectShow Base Classes from the Microsoft Windows Samples, also provided under the MIT License.
* The hand and face detection uses MediaPipe Tasks Vision and the MediaPipe model files, which are published by Google under the Apache License 2.0. They are not stored in this repository and are downloaded by the "npm run vendor" script.
* The other libraries (Tauri, Angular, axum, and the packages listed in the lock files) keep the licenses of their respective authors.
The source code of deck4me is shared publicly for community review and personal contributions under a "Source-Available" model. Any contributions submitted to the repository remain under the copyright of the author unless agreed otherwise.
The application runs on your own computer and processes your webcam image locally. The virtual camera driver is registered on your system with administrator rights, and you are responsible for installing it only on machines you control.

